  "notes": [
    "One object for both Move revisions: the 2010 launch release (CECH-ZCM1) and the current CECH-ZCM2E instruction manual (playstation.com PDF, text by PDFKit) print the same «Approx. 200 mm × 46 mm» labelled «(height × diameter)» and the same 145 g. Mapping: height = 200 (the long axis); the 46 mm is a DIAMETER (of the sphere-topped wand), filed as features.diameter_mm; width and depth stay null, because a diameter is not a labelled width or depth. The manual's label reads «(excluding maximum / projecting part)» across two PDF lines, which sets excludes_projections. Controls from the manual's «Part names» (front and rear views, quoted with the PDF's lines joined): four action buttons (Sony prints them as glyphs, extracted as bare «button») = face_button 4; Move button, PS button, START, SELECT = button 4; T button (the rear trigger) = trigger 1; the sphere is a light, not a control; the pin-hole reset button is not counted. Ports left [] (uncovered): the manual names a «USB connector» without its type (CECH-ZCM1 and ZCM2 differ, mini- vs micro-USB, per secondary sources only). wired=false and cell_kind from the built-in lithium-ion battery line; Move is a wireless motion controller. host_console: the 2010 release introduces it for PlayStation 3 (PS4 and PS VR use it too); key sony-playstation-3-cecha00 (the launch model). The navigation controller (95 g in the same release) is not filed. Status partial: Sony labels only height and diameter, so body width and depth stay null."
  ]
